        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Add about 0.24 seconds. Hand-timed 40s are typically 0.2 to 0.3 seconds faster than electronic times because of human reaction time at the start and finish. A hand-timed 4.50 is roughly a 4.74 electronic."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How do you convert a 40-yard dash time to mph?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Divide 40 yards (36.58 meters) by your time to get meters per second, then multiply by 2.237. A 4.50 second 40 averages about 18.2 mph. Top speed during the run is higher than the average because the first 10 yards are spent accelerating."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What is Speed Score in football?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Speed Score combines 40 time and bodyweight using the formula (weight × 200) ÷ (40 time to the fourth power). It rewards bigger players who run fast. A score near 100 is typical for an NFL running back prospect and 110 or higher is excellent."
