<h2>How This 40-Yard Dash Calculator Works</h2>
<p>Enter your time, pick your position and choose who to compare against. The calculator converts hand times to an electronic equivalent, then estimates your <strong>percentile</strong> using the average and elite (top 10%) times for your position at that level. It also shows your average speed in mph, which NFL positions your time would match, and your <strong>Speed Score</strong> if you add bodyweight.</p>
<p>Benchmarks come from the same data used in our <a href="/average-40-yard-dash-times">average 40-yard dash times by age, position and level</a> guide. Percentiles are estimates, not official rankings.</p>
<h2>Hand-Timed vs. Electronic 40 Times</h2>
<p>Hand-timed 40s usually come out <strong>0.2 to 0.3 seconds faster</strong> than electronic times, because the timer reacts to the start late and stops the watch early. NFL combine times are fully electronic, so this calculator adds <strong>0.24 seconds</strong> to hand times before comparing. A hand-timed 4.45 is really closer to a 4.69 on a laser.</p>
